.git
**/.git

# Build artifacts must never enter the image build context.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . /root/loxilb-io/loxilb/` and then runs the eBPF
# subsystem build with HAVE_HTTP_TRACE=1 HAVE_L4_TRACE=1 HAVE_MTLS=1. A plain
# host-side `make build` sets none of those, so its objects are compiled from
# the same sources with a different feature set. Copied in, they look newer
# than their sources, `make` reports "Nothing to be done", and the image links
# a mix of flag-on and flag-off objects.
#
# That fails as undefined references to the HAVE_HTTP_TRACE-only half of
# sockproxy_trace.c (is_tracing_enabled, emit_trace_event, lxb_should_sample,
# lxb_capture_body_to_tmpfs, lxb_lookup_service_catalog,
# g_catalog_sample_rates) — symbols that have no #else stubs — while
# sockproxy_http.o, which does get rebuilt, references all of them.
#
# Nothing here is tracked in either repo; the container builds all of it from
# source. Excluding it also keeps a ~900 MB working tree from being tarred up
# and shipped to the daemon on every build.
**/*.o
**/*.d
**/*.a
loxilb-ebpf/kernel/loxilb_dp_debug
# The libbpf DESTDIR install tree from host builds: stale host artifacts in
# the context would mask a broken in-image libbpf build (the image rebuilds
# and reinstalls this tree from source every time).
loxilb-ebpf/libbpf/src/build

# The host-built binary; the image builds its own.
/loxilb

# cicd suite run state: root-owned config volumes, staged fixtures and
# evidence written by live scenario runs. Unreadable by the context
# sender (permission denied aborts the build) and never image content.
cicd/**/llb1_config
cicd/**/loxilb.io
cicd/**/artifacts
cicd/**/.certs-stage
cicd/**/.kvprofiles-stage
